(7060706, 1073598, 144271, '<td valign="top">Beautiful well done landscape.  The building looks like it is being swallowed by the fog.</td>', 'Beautiful well done landscape.  The building looks like it is being swallowed by the fog.', '2013-07-04 16:18:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(7060707, 1073836, 144271, '<td valign="top">So well done.  One of the best</td>', 'So well done.  One of the best', '2013-07-04 16:18:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7060711, 1073768, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Black &amp; White tones are just fantastic! Love the viewpoint of these birds taking flight. I feel as if I am standing there observing as they fly overhead. The inclusion of just the one wing that takes prominence in the frame makes this very different than just a shot of birds in the air. It makes it unique in showing off a part of the bird that takes flight while we see all the others soaring above.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Black & White tones are just fantastic! Love the viewpoint of these birds taking flight. I feel as if I am standing there observing as they fly overhead. The inclusion of just the one wing that takes prominence in the frame makes this very different than just a shot of birds in the air. It makes it unique in showing off a part of the bird that takes flight while we see all the others soaring above.', '2013-07-04 16:32:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7060712, 1073410, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow, now that is a sight you don''t see everyday! Great capture of these lionesses stalking the herd. They have each others back while facing down the water buffalo who are turned to face the threat. I do have two little suggestions on how the visual impact of the shot can be improved. First, why not go big to the maximum size limits? Details of the lions and the water buffalo would be more visible and appreciated by the eye. Second I''d have the main subject fill the frame more by cropping out much of the ground plain and some off the sides. That way, we the viewers, get closer to the stalking lionesses and feel more involved in the action by being closer rather that further back and remote.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow, now that is a sight you don''t see everyday! Great capture of these lionesses stalking the herd. They have each others back while facing down the water buffalo who are turned to face the threat. I do have two little suggestions on how the visual impact of the shot can be improved. First, why not go big to the maximum size limits? Details of the lions and the water buffalo would be more visible and appreciated by the eye. Second I''d have the main subject fill the frame more by cropping out much of the ground plain and some off the sides. That way, we the viewers, get closer to the stalking lionesses and feel more involved in the action by being closer rather that further back and remote.', '2013-07-04 16:38:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7060713, 1073397, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I love the mood lighting is these abandoned buildings hallway. It is eerie, spooky and mysterious. My eye is drawn to the vanishing point of this hallway where the the light then tapers off to darkness. This is a good study of light &amp; shadow and mood but I feel like this is more of a foundation or stage for something more to be there - something that will manifest but does not in the frame we are watching. It just needs that extra ''something'' to complete the visual ''story'' of the capture.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I love the mood lighting is these abandoned buildings hallway. It is eerie, spooky and mysterious. My eye is drawn to the vanishing point of this hallway where the the light then tapers off to darkness. This is a good study of light & shadow and mood but I feel like this is more of a foundation or stage for something more to be there - something that will manifest but does not in the frame we are watching. It just needs that extra ''something'' to complete the visual ''story'' of the capture.', '2013-07-04 16:44:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7060714, 1073548, 43463, '<td valign="top">Commented earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Whooo are you looking at? Oh...that would be me:-) Great color and detail in those big orange eyes. He is staring me down, but I get a great look at all the details in this owl''s face down to the downy soft textures of the feathers to the sharp &amp; pointy beak. Well done.</td>', 'Commented earlier coming back to comment. Whooo are you looking at? Oh...that would be me:-) Great color and detail in those big orange eyes. He is staring me down, but I get a great look at all the details in this owl''s face down to the downy soft textures of the feathers to the sharp & pointy beak. Well done.', '2013-07-04 16:46:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7060718, 1073360, 98022, '<td valign="top">Great lighting. Good title.</td>', 'Great lighting. Good title.', '2013-07-04 17:16:24.000000', NULL, 1),
